    "title": "Suspect Flees by Bicycle After Fatal Mar Vista Shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Current Staff ,\n10 hours ago MAR VISTA - A fatal shooting near the intersection of Centinela Avenue and Washington Boulevard sent police to Mar Vista Thursday evening, as a suspect fled by bicycle.\nLos Angeles Police Department officers responded to reports of shots fired at about 5:15 p.m. and found a man in his 40s suffering from a gunshot wound. He was taken to a hospital, where he later died.\nThe suspect left the scene on a bicycle in an unknown direction, according to police. Details about what led to the shooting remain under investigation.\nThe fatal shooting came less than two weeks after a separate shooting near Washington and Centinela prompted a police pursuit that ended in Mar Vista.\nEditor's Note: This story includes reporting from City News Service, a content partner of Westside Current.",
    "summary": "1 hours ago MAR VISTA - A fatal shooting near the intersection of Centinela Avenue and Washington Boulevard sent police to Mar Vista Thursday evening, as a suspect fled by bicycle. Los Angeles Police Department officers responded to reports of shots fired at about 5:15 p.m. and found a man in his 40s suffering from a gunshot wound. The suspect left the scene on a bicycle in an unknown direction, according to police. The fatal shooting came less than two weeks after a separate shooting near Washington and Centinela prompted a police pursuit that ended in Mar Vista.",
